    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήτ-ειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆτος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of sea monsters</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῶτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					2.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένυες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					39.240
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλωρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Perg.</u>
					324.28
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>monstrous</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κήτειοι, οἱ</span>, an unknown race in Mysia, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.521
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				13.1.70
			</span></i>.</div>
